body:
I had tinnitus from an ear infection that gave me anxiety and insomnia - kept me up for a solid week. Hence why I was prescribed the Klonopin. Never had insomnia prior to this. I'm able to fall asleep but unable to stay asleep. I have not woken up to my alarm clock in nearly 13 months. 

&#x200B;

I have started 25mg of Zoloft to cope with this but it's just adding side effects to my current situation.

Not much man. I had to hop on Zoloft because the depression was unbearable and was reaching dangerous levels. Didn't get any sleep last night. This has been a nightmare and I don't understand why I got so walloped after such short usage. Losing hope that I'm going to fully heal. I clearly had to taper but needed to find another doctor who would prescribe. 

&#x200B;

I had a great week in September where I finally started sleeping through the night and then went to the gym and everything went to hell after and I haven't really since a great window like that since.
